				"⡟⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				963,
				137
			],
			"Message": "build(Output): implement complete ESBuild configuration and plugin system\n\nAdd the complete set of ESBuild configuration modules and plugin pipeline source files to Configuration/.\n\nThis includes:\n- ESBuild entry configurations (CodeEditorLand/Editor, CodeEditorLand/Editor, Microsoft/VSCode variants)\n- Plugin pipeline modules (Apply, Copy, Polyfill, Transform namespaces with 50+ transforms)\n- Runtime polyfills (ChildProcess, FileProtocol, FileSystem, IPC/Renderer, SharedProcess, Process, Telemetry)\n- CEL services (ExposeAccessor, TauriMainProcess with MistWebSocketTransport)\n\nAlso add TypeScript composite project configs and polyfill modules.\n\nThe ESBuild configuration supports Rest compiler integration (conditional via Compiler=Rest), PostHog build telemetry (debug-only), target cleanup via Clean=true, and declarative exclusion/transform pipelines that rewrite VS Code's Electron workbench for Tauri/WKWebView compatibility.",
			"SHA": "7604d0318d8f169635792e2a50980d77f0f64453"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-10T15:03:32Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				656,
				126
			],
			"Message": "build(Output): implement Output component ESBuild configuration and pipeline\n\nAdd the complete ESBuild build system source to Configuration/ including: ESBuild entry configurations (Editor, VSCode, Bundle variants), exclusion rule modules (Bootstrap, Electron, Node, Network, Telemetry, Test, Types, WebWorker, Workbench, and Chromium IPC), plugin pipeline (Apply, Copy, Polyfill, Transform namespaces with 50+ transforms), runtime polyfills (ChildProcess, FileProtocol, FileSystem, IPC/Renderer, NativeModule, Process, SharedProcessProxy, Telemetry), and CEL services (ExposeAccessor, ExtensionsScanner, NullExtensionGallery, NullTelemetry, NullUpdate, Search, SharedProcess, DevLog, TauriMainProcess with MistWebSocketTransport, Trace). Also add TypeScript composite project configs for CodeEditorLand/Editor and Microsoft/VSCode targets.\n\nThese modules were previously only present as compiled .js/.js.map outputs in Configuration/ - the authoritative source now lives in the repository enabling reproducible builds, source-level debugging of the build pipeline, and version-controlled evolution of the Output component's bundling logic. The ESBuild configuration supports Rest compiler integration (conditional via Compiler=Rest), PostHog build telemetry (debug-only), target cleanup via Clean=true, and declarative exclusion/transform pipelines that rewrite VS Code's Electron workbench for Tauri/WKWebView compatibility.",
			"SHA": "d2876e62d1224ae346a27e4d080c5b2f9f0c053f"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-10T14:47:59Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				344,
				4
			],
			"Message": "build(Output): Remove compiled Configuration artifacts and normalize Source formatting\n\nDelete all generated ESBuild output files (.js and .js.map) from the Configuration/ directory that were previously checked into version control. The Configuration/ directory is the ESBuild outdir for bundled artifacts consumed by Cocoon at runtime — these are build outputs, not source.\n\nRetain and reformat the authoritative Source/ modules: Source/ESBuild/Output.js (entry point with RestPlugin conditional loading, PostHog build telemetry, target cleanup logic) and tsconfig.json (composite project config extending @playform/build). Both files normalized to compact spacing without inter-statement blank lines.\n\nThis ensures the repository tracks only source-of-truth configuration while Cocoon continues to consume fresh builds from Configuration/ at runtime via the existing build pipeline.",
			"SHA": "84fffb908dc959d20c954bc98fd6fd29acedf738"
		}
	],
